A soulstone holds what a cleric draws out of the dead, and a bolsterer
spends it on armor.

Its level runs one to ten and decides two things: how much a single rite
puts into it, and how much it can hold at all.  A stone deepens when it holds
a hundred charges for each level it already has, and never falls back.
Spending does not cost it a level, but the charges spent have to be earned
again before it deepens.

Stones are made by a shaman out of an opal, and the size of the opal decides
where the stone starts.

